    "created_at": "2026-11-09T21:12:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T21:12:47Z",
    "body": "**Checked on a real project.** The contributor ran the GUI on `test-423.camproj` (two setups; Face top and Hole 6mm in Setup1, Outside profile in Setup2). The post-options half was then driven headlessly through this branch's own commands on that same file.\n\n**GUI (contributor, hands-on)**\n- Setup1's Tool list page lists its 2 tools in change order, with time estimates.\n- **Export tool list…** wrote `Setup1-tools.csv` (`T,Tool,Diameter mm,Kind,Holder,Operations`, one row per tool) and a fixed-column `.txt` (`TOOL LIST - Setup1` … `2 tool(s)`). The status line confirmed each write.\n- Setup2's tool list shows its 1 tool.\n\n**Per-setup post options (commands on the real file; every operation given a program stop after it)**\n| Step | Stops posted (Face top / Hole 6mm / Outside profile) |\n|---|---|\n| Baseline | ✓ ✓ ✓ |\n| `SetSetupPostOptions(Setup1, own, skip pauses and homes)` | ✗ ✗ ✓. Setup2 follows the document and keeps its stop |\n| Same, with Setup2 active | ✗ ✗ ✓. Each op reads its own setup's switch |\n| Save → reopen | Setup1 keeps its own options; Setup2 still follows |\n| Undo | Setup1 follows the document again; the post is byte-identical to the baseline |\n\nThe PR's suites: app `setup_post_options` 8/8 and ui lib `setup_post_options` 3/3.\n\n**Not exercised:** clicking the Post page radio and checkbox by hand. `the_post_page_radio_gives_the_setup_its_own_options` covers it through the UI state.\n\nMarking ready for review (contributor OK).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
