    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T21:45:44Z",
    "body": "Review fix pushed (`7fa0fbee`, merged current main). Besides the module-list conflicts, a semantic merge with #155 and #388:\n- `program_entry::posted_afters` now takes a per-op skip predicate, so each op's after-action follows its own setup's \"Skip pauses and homes\". A Pause/Home entry folding into a skipping op's gap is muted with it (it cannot refuse), and an entry ahead of every posted op follows the first posted op's switch.\n- The Output/thread agreement check moved from the retired one-mount clause into the program gate. It stays program-wide (stricter than #388's per-mount files), as noted in the decision record.\n\nNew pin: `setup_post_options::an_entry_in_a_skipping_setups_gap_is_muted_with_its_op`. A Go-home entry after Setup2's stop refuses the program until Setup2 skips; then Setup1 keeps its stop and Setup2's op and its entry are muted, and undo restores the refusal.\n\nMerged tree: `setup_post_options` 9/9, `program_entry` 7/7, `posting` 17, `per_op_files` 9, `after_op` 10, `conformance` 6, `setup_mount` 6, `setup_mounts_post` 5, ui `setup_post_options` 3 and `structural` 3, all passing; clippy on app+ui clean. Fork synced at v0.15.0. Stays a draft until it is flagged ready again.",
